# provision/

Instance topology for `qctl vm` / `qctl local` / seed. Pick a **profile** with
`-p` / `--profile` (default from `common.yaml`).

## Files

| File | Put here |
|------|----------|
| `common.yaml` | Shared settings + `qctl.environments` / `qctl.profiles` / `qctl.default-profile` |
| `target-<target>.yaml` | Defaults for a hypervisor (`workstation` or `proxmox`) |
| `env-<env>.yaml` | Settings shared by every profile that uses that env |
| `profile-<profile>.yaml` | Settings for one profile (wins last) |
| `.env.schema` + `.env.<env>` | Host secrets for `!env` (optional `.env.local`, gitignored) |

Merge order (later wins; maps merge, arrays replace):

`common.yaml` → `target-*.yaml` → `env-*.yaml` → `profile-*.yaml`

At least one of those four YAML files must exist.

## Common tasks

- **Disks** — `disks:` (`os` / `data` / `tanks`). Encrypted tank passphrase:
  `disks.tanks.<id>.passphrase: !env NAME`. Create pools with `qctl vm init-tank`
  (appliance boot only imports/unlocks).
- **SSH / users / repo** — optional under `ssh:`, `users:`, `repo:` (same `!env`
  graph). Omit `users:` to get defaults (admin uid 1000, apps uid 900).
- **Networking** — `networking.ports` / `uplinks` / `vlans` (see
  [docs/provision.md](../../docs/provision.md) in the qctl repo, or your team docs).

## Not in this folder

VM images, seed ISOs, and disk images live under XDG cache/data
(`~/.cache/qctl/`, `~/.local/share/qctl/`), not in the instance repo.
